:0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.03596245979163992,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":54.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.07521374602452968,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":62.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03812591062213971,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":53.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.04582780275374232,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0049531459170013385,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.032679997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":21.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"White Mountains Insurance Group, Ltd. provides insurance services in the United States, the United Kingdom, Bermuda, and internationally. It operates through Ark/WM Outrigger, HG Global, Kudu, Distinguished, and Other Operations segments. The company offers property insurance and reinsurance; specialty insurance and reinsurance consisting of aviation, contingency, cyber, fine art and specie, mortgage, nuclear, political and credit, space, surety, and terrorism and political violence; marine and energy insurance and reinsurance; casualty insurance and reinsurance, such as medical malpractice, and professional and general liability; and accident and health insurance and reinsurance, which includes personal accident, sickness, disability, travel, short-term life, and medical products through brokers, managing general agents (MGA), and reinsurance intermediaries. It also provides municipal bond guarantee reinsurance, which focuses on single risk limits for small-to-medium sized, and public investment grade municipal bonds that are issued to finance public purpose projects, including schools, utilities, and transportation facilities. In addition, the company offers capital solutions for boutique asset and wealth managers for generational ownership transfers, management buyouts, acquisition and growth finance, and legacy partner liquidity; strategic advice; investment management; and specialty electrical contracting services. Further, it operates as a full-service MGA and program administrator for specialty property and casualty insurance for the real estate and hospitality end markets, and start-up programs; and an MGA for leisure travel and global expatriate medical insurance in Israel, the European Union, and Australia. The company was formerly known as Fund American Enterprises Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to White Mountains Insurance Group, Ltd. in 1999. White Mountains Insurance Group, Ltd. was incorporated in 1980 and is headquartered in Hamilton, Bermuda.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Liam P. Caffrey | CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $2.3M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["White Mountains Insurance Group is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.4B market cap on $3.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +48% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 18\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $92.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves roo